uxCriticalNesting starts at 0xaaaaaaaa rather than 0.

The word at 0x20007208 is in .data with that value, as the kernel's own port has
it, and xPortStartScheduler zeroes it. Before the scheduler runs, a critical
section therefore leaves BASEPRI raised when it exits, because the count never
reaches zero, so no kernel-aware interrupt runs until the first task does.

--- a/CMSIS/nrf52/port_cmsis.c
+++ b/CMSIS/nrf52/port_cmsis.c
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 
 /* Each task maintains its own interrupt status in the critical nesting
 variable. */
-static UBaseType_t uxCriticalNesting = 0;
+static UBaseType_t uxCriticalNesting = 0xaaaaaaaa;
 
